1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,283
Good morning everyone. I'm Steve Wainwright,

2
00:00:03,283 --> 00:00:08,910
from Elmleigh Town Council, and I organise the town's volunteer scheme.

3
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:12,700
I'm delighted you're all interested in joining the scheme.

4
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:17,959
Our volunteers help to create a sense of community among the many people

5
00:00:17,959 --> 00:00:21,380
who live in our historic town of Elmleigh, and make residents

6
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:25,240
and visitors feel welcome at local events.

7
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:30,980
First I'll mention just a few of the activities that volunteers carry out.

8
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:37,090
One is to walk around the town centre streets wearing our volunteer T-shirt.

9
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:40,995
Tourists often ask how to get to a particular shop,

10
00:00:40,995 --> 00:00:45,680
and they might also be grateful for recommendations about what to visit.

11
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:49,338
The town holds a large number of concerts each year,

12
00:00:49,338 --> 00:00:57,020
and part of the volunteers' role is to get everyone in the audience to the right place as smoothly as possible.

13
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:01,445
You'd be surprised how many people buy tickets then don't check them,

14
00:01:01,445 --> 00:01:04,290
and head for the wrong section of the hall!

15
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:07,980
Volunteers may get involved with community groups

16
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:12,290
such as sports clubs or gardeners' associations.

17
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:17,050
Here the volunteers talk about how groups can help each other.

18
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:24,415
For instance, a writing group might want to travel to another town to hear a talk by a well-known author,

19
00:01:24,415 --> 00:01:29,570
but may not know that another club has a coach they could travel in.

20
00:01:29,570 --> 00:01:31,600
The town produces a monthly magazine

21
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:36,290
and anyone who lives in the town can send in articles.

22
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:38,374
It's free to residents,

23
00:01:38,374 --> 00:01:40,100
and is paid for by local businesses

24
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:45,460
that's the responsibility of the council's advertising department.

25
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:47,298
We depend on volunteers, though,

26
00:01:47,298 --> 00:01:50,620
to find out what people think of events they've attended

27
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:54,280
and any suggestions they have for the future.

28
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,490
The volunteers then send a summary to the editors.

29
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:01,664
There are a number of clubs for retired people,

30
00:02:02,368 --> 00:02:07,250
and every year, the council arranges lunch for all the members

31
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:08,940
The volunteers welcome the guests

32
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:13,245
and when everyone's sitting down and relaxing after the meal,

33
00:02:13,245 --> 00:02:14,800
some volunteers put on a show

34
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:19,240
usually around half an hour of songs and short plays.

35
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:25,170
The club members really welcome the chance to chat to the volunteers at these events.

36
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:27,390
The town council has a website,

37
00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:32,940
of course, and volunteers are asked to help by making sure residents know about it.

38
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:36,550
It's updated every day with information about future activities,

39
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:40,520
and we want as many people as possible to use it.

40
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:44,500
OK, now you know some of the things our volunteers do

41
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:48,430
I'll go on to some practical matters.

42
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:53,235
As you probably know, the town arranges three major festivals every year,

43
00:02:53,235 --> 00:02:57,240
and they all depend on a large number of volunteers.

44
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,520
The book festival lasts three days

45
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:03,430
and uses several venues, which all need volunteers.

46
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:07,515
More are needed for the music festival, because that lasts a whole week,

47
00:03:07,515 --> 00:03:10,340
and even more help is required for the science festival

48
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:13,170
even though it's only two days long.

49
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:16,630
It involves quite a lot of venues, though.

50
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:21,184
It's a good idea to help at the festival you're most interested in,

51
00:03:21,184 --> 00:03:24,220
because you can attend most of the events for free.

52
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,280
We try to use volunteers who are flexible, though

53
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,873
because some festival events are held outdoors,

54
00:03:29,873 --> 00:03:32,740
and the weather may affect the size of the audience

55
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:36,233
and even whether the event can take place;

56
00:03:36,233 --> 00:03:39,060
so there can be changes at short notice.

57
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:45,236
What's essential, though, is being able to get on well with other people,

58
00:03:45,236 --> 00:03:50,970
and also to deal with someone who's behaving badly - as occasionally happens.

59
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:54,300
Our plan is to get you all working in September

60
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:57,710
after a week's training starting on the 2nd.

61
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:03,170
So we'll be timetabling you for duties the following week, from the 9th onward.

62
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:08,768
Later, in the week beginning September 23rd, we have a chat with each of you,

63
00:04:08,768 --> 00:04:14,740
to find out how you feel about being a volunteer, and what extra support you need.

64
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:19,730
As a thank you to the volunteers, we arrange an annual event.

65
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:23,060
In recent years we've had a party in the town hall

66
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:27,250
and last year a barbecue in Chamber Park.

67
00:04:27,250 --> 00:04:32,490
Our forthcoming event is a trip along the canal from here to Dewhurst and back.

68
00:04:32,490 --> 00:04:36,580
It's on Saturday September the 28th, and if you'd like to attend

69
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:39,210
you can sign up once you start work.

70
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:43,250
Now this is the volunteers' T-shirt...
